Z||000003||ArmandoP||11-29-2000||11:26 PM||||thanks, Ill fix the siggy right away....<P>its going to be mid to late summer.  this gives people a chance to get off from work to drive up and get money together and plan for it, etc etc.<P>Its a road course...not a drag strip or an oval.....the the best of both worlds....fully insured with instructors if you would like to have them give you info I believe!<BR>Armando<P>------------------<BR>__________________<BR>will work for MR2 parts!!! <BR>1987 MR2 NA t-bar csp with 700 miles on its new engine. <BR>TRD copper head gasket, milled head .020, 2 short shifters,metal masters rear brake pads, 195-60-14 (soon to get new tires), clear corners, Clevite 77 bearings, NO A/C, MAF relocation mod, red silicon vacuum hoses, redline tranny fluid,and the stock exhaust with a WHOLE bunch of broken welds! <BR>indiana/illinois MR2 owners club<BR>[URL]http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/inimoc.html [/URL]<BR>[IMG] <A HREF="http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/4age.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/4age.jpg</A>  [/IMG]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||11-29-2000||11:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ArmandoP:<BR><B>Its a road course...with instructors</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Oooh, a road course!!! I'm salivating.<P>BTW... we don't need no stinking instructors.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ArmandoP||11-29-2000||11:41 PM||||well, Im not sure on how the istructor bit goes.....  I think ts mainly to keep people from doing stupid stuff....<BR>remember, its not a competition, just a chance for car lovers to get together and drive a real track.  I can still guarantee my car willl be the ugliest one there....but hey, atleast my engine looks good. hehehe<BR>:-)<BR>Armando||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||11-29-2000||11:44 PM||||doh.. I wish I lived closer... otherwise I'd definitely be there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I wouldn't mind having instructors.. I received fairly good training when I took the Young Drivers course, but there was a lot they never taught me.. such as how to safely spin a car 180*....<P>and sure, it's easy to say "just don't do that"... I've tried it before, but only managed a bit less than 90* on dry pavement.. it's easy on ice, but hard to control... same with gravel. I want to learn stuff like that so I can do it safely..<P>are there any driving schools where you can learn stuff like that??<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
