Z||000017||ArmandoP||12-19-2000||02:20 PM||||OK,<BR>it is open to any cars assumiung that havingthose cars run will not cause our insurance to go up.  I know that transams and camaros will not be allowed, as well as vipers.  I do know that all variations of mr2 and fiero are welcome, as well as Miatas.<BR>I havent checked on it, but I think the Cobra would probably raise our rates.  safety is the number one issue for me in planning this, so I want to make sure that the insurance will be in effect and that nothing we do causes it to be null.<BR>IT is  $150 to run the course for the day.  IF you dont wish to run the course, but still want to xcome and enjoy the food, people, displsyas from the sponsors, etc e5tc etc...it is a $10 fee to cover the costs. IF, which I seriously doubt, we have any money left over, then that will go owards the illianaMOC, the illiana mr2 owners club. We are the ones hosting the event, so I think thats only fair.  though, keep in mind.  it is almost $6000 to rent the track, so we will probably NOT have any mney left over.<P>From what I know, there will be three classes. Novice, intermediate and experienced.  Based on your experience is how they determine the intervention of an instrunctor...though intervention isnt eally the right word.<BR>if you are brand new to this, expect to have several laps with an instructor, if you have some experience,the that time goes down and free runs on the track go up.  if you are experienced, then they probably will hjust turn you loose with your group.<BR>Main thing is we dont want somebody out there who thinks they know whats up, then all of a sudden realize they dont and they end up mangling their car, the track and god forbid themselves.  So, safety is numnber one.  Honestly, this is the opnly way to do it and keep it affordable.<BR>I will be making a lit of people as soon as we come up with a date the first of the year.  it will be mid to late suymmer.<BR>Armando<P>------------------<BR>__________________<BR>will work for MR2 parts!!! <BR>1987 MR2 NA t-bar csp with 700 miles on its new engine. <BR>TRD copper head gasket, milled head .020, 2 short shifters,metal masters rear brake pads, 195-60-14 (soon to get new tires), clear corners, Clevite 77 bearings, NO A/C, MAF relocation mod, red silicon vacuum hoses, redline tranny fluid,and the stock exhaust with a WHOLE bunch of broken welds! <BR>indiana/illinois MR2 owners club<BR>[URLhttp://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/inimoc.html[/URL]<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/mytwo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Tina||12-19-2000||11:56 PM||||<P>Any chance of a dragstrip<BR>                     event coming up in the near future? <P>Try'd to get something like that going in MN<BR>Still time,too. <BR>But the response was rather disapointing.<P>Hope the gingerbread is a go.<BR>And lots of pics please,just too far to go to.<P>Tina||||reg||1
